TOTAL atomic=27 compound=1

Discussion:
The Vehicle State category has 27 atomic fields and 1 compound (DoorState).
The compound is never dispatched — internal/tesla/codec/flatten.go's
flattenDoorStateJSON expands it into 6 boolean atomics at codec time:
DoorStateDriverFront, DoorStateDriverRear, DoorStatePassengerFront,
DoorStatePassengerRear, DoorStateFrontTrunk, DoorStateRearTrunk.

The DoorState JSON wire shape uses FrontTrunk/RearTrunk (NOT TrunkFront/
TrunkRear, which is the proto Doors message naming used by flattenDoors).
The codec preserves the producer's field names verbatim — the divergence
is real (it is the upstream's design) and obscuring it would silently
corrupt provenance for any operator inspecting signal_log. This routing
prompt therefore registers the codec-emitted names verbatim, not aliased
left/right names.

Routing decisions:
  * 25 of 27 atomics route to signal_log (low-cardinality state with
    no hot column: window state, light state, software update progress,
    homelink, guest mode, tonneau, current speed-limit setting, odometer,
    paired phone count, software version, etc.).
  * SentryMode + ValetModeEnabled route to security_event — every
    transition is a discrete security-relevant event; the writer diffs
    against the previous observation and emits one row per transition.
  * ServiceMode routes to safety_snapshot.service_mode (continuous-value
    flag, see migrations/000170_snapshots_si.up.sql:312).
  * 6 DoorState flatten atomics route to signal_log per the prompt's
    routing rule (low-cardinality change-feed analytics; transitions
    surface on the security timeline through the security_events writer
    reading from signal_log, not via direct router dispatch).

No classifier ambiguity:
  * pm.Signals shows ZERO vehicle_state fields that overlap any prior
    routed category. Soc (mentioned defensively in the prompt) is in
    Category=charging and was routed by prompt 0040; it is NOT in the
    vehicle_state pm.Signals slice. ServiceMode is uniquely in
    vehicle_state (safety_security category does not include it).
  * The routing.yaml loader's duplicate-field validator
    (TestLoaderRejectsDuplicateField) provides structural enforcement;
    no duplicates were introduced by this prompt.

